            rf"(and, in the second column, 12 lags of the monthly averages of the $r^*$-gap yield and FCI); all controls are dated before month $t$ and the contemporaneous FCI is not included. January 1996 to September 2026, nothing dropped. The coefficient is divided by the window slope of the yield on the surprise ({r0.window_slope:.2f}), "
